Start with a read-only audit. Then report the proposed tests, simulations, files to create, and commands to execute.

Do not modify the live robot, run motors, reboot the Raspberry Pi, change system services, charge or discharge batteries, or conduct physical experiments.

Do not install packages, deploy code, overwrite existing files, commit changes, or push to GitHub without my explicit approval.

Never expose credentials or secrets.

Once I approve a proposed offline testing and analysis plan, execute the approved work, preserve original evidence, and report the actual outputs and any failures.

Your objective is to maximize genuine, reproducible scientific evidence—not to manufacture impressive-looking results.

Begin with the full repository audit and return the prioritized execution plan first.
